<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ private sector earnings up 3.7 pct in August yr.</title>
<headline>NZ private sector earnings up 3.7 pct in August yr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following information from the August quarterly employment survey was released by Statistics New Zealand on Tuesday:</p>
<p>Ordinary time average hourly earnings, change from same period of previous year:</p>
<p>Total</p>
<p>		     Aug 1996 yr     May 1996 yr   Aug 1995 yr</p>
<p>NZ$		  $16.08	    $15.97	  $15.55</p>
<p>Pct change	 3.4		 3.4	     2.7</p>
<p>Private sector</p>
<p>		     Aug 1996 yr    May 1996 yr   Aug 1995 yr</p>
<p>NZ$		  $15.41	    $15.36	  $14.86</p>
<p>Pct change	 3.7		 4.0	     2.6</p>
<p>Public sector</p>
<p>		     Aug 1996 yr    May 1996 yr   Aug 1995 yr</p>
<p>NZ$		  $18.06	    $17.77	  $17.51</p>
<p>Pct change	 3.1		 2.2	     3.9</p>
<p>Ordinary time average hourly earnings, percentage change from same period of previous quarter:  </p>
<p>		     Aug 1996 qtr    May 1996 qtr  Aug 1995 qtr</p>
<p>Private sector   0.3 pct	   1.5 pct	 0.6 pct</p>
<p>Public sector    1.6 pct	   0.2 pct	 0.7 pct</p>
<p>Total		0.7 pct	   1.1 pct	 0.6 pct</p>
<p>Jobs filled:</p>
<p>		     Aug 1996	 May 1996	 Aug 1995</p>
<p>Full Time (million)  1.08	     1.07	     1.04</p>
<p>Part Time (million)  0.43	     0.42	     0.42</p>
<p>Total (million)	1.51	     1.49	     1.46</p>
<p>Note economists had forecast private sector average ordinary time earnings would rise 4.2 percent in the August year, and total ordinary time earnings 3.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
